=====================

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SNMP vendor device-profiles
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The SNMP vendor device-profiles (src/backend/snmp_profiles_seed.go and
src/config/snmp_profiles.json) are ORIGINAL to this project. Their OID/metric
definitions are compiled directly from the vendors' published SNMP MIBs and the
relevant IETF RFC MIBs (IF-MIB, HOST-RESOURCES-MIB, ENTITY-MIB, BGP4-MIB,
OSPF-MIB, and per-vendor enterprise MIBs). OIDs are factual identifiers defined
in those MIBs. No third-party profile catalog is bundled.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Active Verification troubleshooting modules — knowledge mined from NetClaw
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The troubleshooting KNOWLEDGE behind the Active Verification modules
(src/backend/verify_modules.go — per-vendor read-only command selection and the
fault indicators the deterministic parsers look for: CRC/input-error semantics,
duplex-mismatch and interface-flap indicators, BGP session-reset / prefix-
collapse diagnosis, and config-change-before-incident causality) is derived
from the skill procedures of the NetClaw project:

  Project : NetClaw, by John Capobianco
  Source  : https://github.com/automateyournetwork/netclaw
  License : Apache License 2.0
  Pinned  : commit 49332542f43390955e758b69855a111b5ba0ff4c
  Skills  : pyats-troubleshoot, pyats-health-check, pyats-routing,
            pyats-junos-interfaces, pyats-junos-routing, junos-network

No NetClaw code, agent runtime, or LLM component is bundled or executed — only
the distilled troubleshooting procedures, re-expressed as this project's own
closed command tables and deterministic parsers. The Arista EOS, Nokia SR OS
and Huawei VRP command profiles are original to this project (NetClaw does not
cover those CLIs).
